{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/460954-\u200btheory-bale-hounds-as-effects-of-christianity","id":460954,"title":"\u200bTheory: Bale Hounds as effects of Christianity","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-03-29T05:56:43-07:00","id":460954,"title":"\u200bTheory: Bale Hounds as effects of Christianity","content":"We know that in Europe the biggest problem for the Forsaken are Bale Hounds, not the Pure Tribes. ( See <b>Shadows of UK</b> on this ) The rouge packs of Maeljin worshippers are everywhere in Old World, between large cities. Seeing how mine private game unfolded, I come to bold theory \u2013 <b>Bale Hounds are plague of Europe because of Christianity.</b><br /> <br /> Think on this pre-Christian European cultures are very animistic in their outlook \u2013 they are direct animists or polytheists, with various lesser god and spirits filling the niche of Shadow Realm. Previous notion of werewolf was still as a monster, sure, but not the \u201cdemon\u201d without the soul the Church cast it in early Middle Ages. They were most often cursed man. Werewolf were sometimes \u201cblessed\u201d even ( like <i><a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Berserker\" target=\"_blank\">\u00dalfh\u00e9\u00f0nar</a> </i>in Vikings culture ). It\u2019s stable of working for the \u201cdark forces\u201d ( animistic faiths ) cast Uratha as \u201cbeyond redemption\u201d in the eyes of the Church, and later, Christians in general.<br /> <br /> And then, when devoted Christian, become the werewolf after First Change, his whole life teachings pointed him that he <b>is</b> the monster and works for the Satan. In that light, it\u2019s understandable that most Uratha who would not be guided by the elders from the Tribes of Moon or Pure would sooner or later becoming part of Bale Hounds, having to resolve their spiritual and flesh needs, stirred by the Lords of Wounds to their service.<br /> <br /> What do you think about it?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-29T09:30:52-07:00","id":461102,"title":"","content":"Lol dunno if Id use terms like bold and theory. That's essentially the facts of it from shadows of the Uk.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> WoD-Dark Eras!! (Backed for Viking Age Werewolf)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1939-lyrics-of-war","name":"Lyrics Of War","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1939_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1769"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-29T10:40:37-07:00","id":461216,"title":"","content":"I think it has to do more with the fact that WW2 completely thrashed Europe, opened an incredible huge amount of Wounds and people finds it easier to work with the status quo than to say, challenge Hell itself. YMMV.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-29T14:56:37-07:00","id":461516,"title":"","content":"That situation certainly didn't help, but I recall reading that the uk has a massive amount of bale hounds due to the pervasive belief of werewolf = devil worship. Any uratha not in the know may easily be convinced they're a hell demon by any spirit aligned with the maeljin. Never mind that there's roving packs of these mongrels.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> WoD-Dark Eras!! (Backed for Viking Age Werewolf)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1939-lyrics-of-war","name":"Lyrics Of War","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1939_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1769"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-29T15:56:36-07:00","id":461612,"title":"","content":"It might work historcially, but in modern days I just don't see it. In Britain particularly, being religious is really a niche hobby. A majority identify as Christian, but I'd guess that most people probably couldn't tell you much about it.<br /> <br /> It also doesn't explain why this isn't an issue in the Americas. Most people there are Christian, and it actually has a degree of cultural relevance in large areas.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-30T02:09:32-07:00","id":462035,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/460954-\u200btheory-bale-hounds-as-effects-of-christianity?p=461612#post461612\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It might work historcially, but in modern days I just don't see it. In Britain particularly, being religious is really a niche hobby. A majority identify as Christian, but I'd guess that most people probably couldn't tell you much about it.</div> </div> </div> </div>What once started from Christianity, get more impetus with each generation of Bale Hounds packs in the wild. And Europeans started to turn away from Christianity only in late Victorian era. And then we have WW 1 and WW 2, working for Maeljins...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/460954-\u200btheory-bale-hounds-as-effects-of-christianity?p=461612#post461612\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It also doesn't explain why this isn't an issue in the Americas. Most people there are Christian, and it actually has a degree of cultural relevance in large areas.</div> </div> </div> </div>Americas have Native animistic cultures that sinked a bit in to overall outlook of Colonies. Yes, most time second and third generation Americans did not worship the Spirits of Indians, but were easily more convinced &quot;those are pagan gods and their Hunting Grounds&quot; than &quot;Hisil is literal Hell&quot;. Europeans did not have those animistic beliefs in open from 10th century onward.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 10-31-2018, 03:29 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-30T02:48:41-07:00","id":462044,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> What once started from Christianity, get more impetus with each generation of Bale Hounds packs in the wild. And Europeans started to turn away from Christianity only in late Victorian era. And then we have WW 1 and WW 2, working for Maeljins... </div> </div> </div>Ah, that makes more sense.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Americas have Native animistic cultures that sinked a bit in to overall outlook of Colonies. </div> </div> </div>Well, it depends where you go. South and Central America where much of the pre-Columbian peoples and culture carried on I'll give you. But the United States? I don't think that works.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Europeans did not have those animistic believes in open from X century onward. </div> </div> </div>I'd say it'd be more likely the Reformation Era. Medieval people weren't all that bothered by the Devil.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-30T04:04:40-07:00","id":462080,"title":"","content":"All right, but if bale hounds were the result of christians not having another frame of reference when they became werewolves, what's the excuse now?<br /> <br /> People have had werewolf movies for almost 75 years now. So for the last three generations, people are more likely to believe their lycanthropy was a gypsy curse than a sign that they're chosen by Satan, especially since the number of christians who believe that satan makes werewolves would have to be very very small. <br /> <br /> Why isn't the lodge of the gypsy curse the problem of europe instead of bale hounds?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-30T06:03:09-07:00","id":462149,"title":"","content":"Note to self: Spam Azocrotarim to make a &quot;Lodge of the Gypsy Curse&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-30T06:16:09-07:00","id":462164,"title":"","content":"There are probably places in Europe where more people believe in werewolves <i>than</i> Satan.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-31T00:00:59-07:00","id":463174,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/460954-\u200btheory-bale-hounds-as-effects-of-christianity?p=462149#post462149\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Note to self: Spam Azocrotarim to make a &quot;Lodge of the Gypsy Curse&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div> Yes, while it wasn't a serious suggestion, but thinking about it, yeah if there can be a lodge who thinks werewolves are cursed by Zeus there's no reason why there wouldn't be a lodge with a far more modern take on things.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}